        "notes": "The colour of Gaia DR3's measured spectrum of the star: a white F-type star, a little warmer than Beta Pictoris. The darkening toward the edge is the quadratic law Claret and Bloemen (2011) compute from ATLAS model atmospheres for a star of 7,422 K and log g 4.31: a model, because no image measures this star's limb. The star is 0.45 milliarcseconds across, which the CHARA interferometer measures as a size only (Elliott et al. 2024). No spin axis is measured, so the display axis is celestial north."
